bic_trace_step.reason:
The function `pci_dev_reset_iommu_done()` introduced in this commit attempts to re-attach the device to `group->domain` in lines 4016-4019: 
c
	/* Re-attach RID domain back to group->domain */
	if (group->domain != group->blocking_domain) {
		WARN_ON(__iommu_attach_device(group->domain, &pdev->dev,
						      group->blocking_domain));
	}

If `group->domain` is NULL (which can happen if default domain allocation failed), the condition `group->domain != group->blocking_domain` evaluates to true, and `__iommu_attach_device` is called with a NULL domain pointer, leading to a NULL pointer dereference.
